9185/state.json" "file_sha256" "1788a635c8e0149bcea3899eb9366c7fa8a9fae36dac0f57f6ebf6083588e2ca"} {"question" "q-333213" "field" "field-3" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/select "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14069185/state.json" "file_sha256" "1788a635c8e0149bcea3899eb9366c7fa8a9fae36dac0f57f6ebf6083588e2ca"} {"question" "q-333213" "field" "field-3" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "a saddle point"] ["text" "a stable node (sink)"] ["text" "an unstable node (source)"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14069185/state.json" "file_sha256" "1788a635c8e0149bcea3899eb9366c7fa8a9fae36dac0f57f6ebf6083588e2ca"} {"question" "q-333213" "field" "field-3" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "a saddle point"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14069185/state.json" "file_sha256" "1788a635c8e0149bcea3899eb9366c7fa8a9fae36dac0f57f6ebf6083588e2ca"} {"question" "q-333224" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}^{′}(t)=-2x(t) \\\\ {y}^{′}(t)=-4y(t)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSelect the correct options below regarding the given decoupled system of linear differential equations.$\\,$\nThe $x$-axis is a {{field-1}} line.\n\n$\\,$\nThe $y$-axis is a {{field-2}} line.\n\n$\\,$\nThe equilibrium point (origin) is {{field-3}}." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14069185/state.json" "file_sha256" "1788a635c8e0149bcea3899eb9366c7fa8a9fae36dac0f57f6ebf6083588e2ca"} {"question" "q-333224" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Writing our system in matrix form, we have\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -4\\end{aligned}]x(t)\n$$\n\nwhere $x(t)=[\\begin{aligned}x(t) \\\\ y(t)\\end{aligned}].$\n\nRecall that a homogeneous system of linear differential equations has a single equilibrium (fixed point) at the origin.\n\nSince our system is decoupled, its eigenvectors are the following:\n\n- Eigenvalue ${\\lambda }_{1}=-2$ with the eigenvector $[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}].$ The corresponding straight-line solutions of the form\n${c}_{1}{e}^{-2t}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]$\nlie on the $x$-axis and approach the origin as $t\\to \\infty .$ So, the $x$-axis is the $\\text{stable}$ line.\n\n- Eigenvalue ${\\lambda }_{2}=-4$ with the eigenvector $[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].$ The corresponding straight-line solutions of the form\n${c}_{2}{e}^{-4t}[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]$\nlie on the $y$-axis and also approach the origin as $t\\to \\infty .$ So, the $y$-axis is the $\\text{stable}$ line.\n\nTherefore, the equilibrium point (origin) is $\\text{a stable node (sink)}.$ \n\n**Note:** The phase portrait of the system looks as follows:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14069185/assets/062b58a307f6d40c7be59d527cc01d7d301bd3f0115a0074ba0f3dca54412425.png)" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14069185/state.json" "file_sha256" "1788a635c8e0149bcea3899eb9366c7fa8a9fae36dac0f57f6ebf6083588e2ca"} {"question" "q-333224" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14069185/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "727c6876100d08ae032659276e3b453d2d1ae8fed06910a1a96a7ea6adbd89b2"} {"question" "q-333224" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/select "